          "content": "B\n\n**Explanation:** \nThe decision rests on maximizing overall well-being and minimizing net suffering. The $5,000 relieves intense, prolonged financial distress and prevents months of severe deprivation, providing a substantial increase in well-being. In contrast, the homeowner suffers only a minor, temporary reduction in comfort\u2014a postponed vacation\u2014while their essential needs and financial security remain completely intact. Because the marginal benefit of that money to someone in debt far exceeds the marginal harm to someone with ample savings, this outcome produces the greater net good.",
